# What the image build must never see.
#
# Secrets first: keys/ and .env are instance state generated by install.sh.
# A COPY that includes them would bake them into a build-stage layer — not the
# final image, but any layer is one `docker history --no-trunc` away.
keys/
backups/
.env
.env.local
docker-compose.override.yml

# Build artefacts. The dashboard is built by the Dockerfile's node stage from
# web/src — a stale local build must not leak into the context, and
# web/node_modules alone would multiply the context size by orders of
# magnitude for nothing (the stage runs npm ci itself).
bin/
dist/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.angular/
*.out
coverage.html

# History is not an input: the VERSION build arg carries what the binary needs.
.git/
